{"ts": 1793977971.059811, "run_id": "bradford_sample__prompt_only__claude-haiku-5-5__r2__3d94afc43900", "source": "agent", "event": "assistant_text", "text": "I ran the Bradford assay on the unknown protein sample and read the plate at 595 nm. Well A1 reads 0.3207 absorbance.\n\nWhat I did:\n1. Picked up a tip (tips:A1) and transferred 10 \u00b5L of the unknown protein sample (reagents:A4) into assay_plate:A1, then dropped the tip.\n2. Picked up a fresh tip (tips:A2), since the first one had touched the sample source, and transferred 200 \u00b5L of Bradford dye reagent (reagents:A3) into assay_plate:A1, then dropped the tip.\n3. Read assay_plate at 595 nm.\n\nThe other 95 wells read about 0.03\u20130.06, which is background. A1 is the only well with signal, and its 0.3207 reading is the sample.\n\nI did not run a BSA standard curve, so this reading is not yet converted to a protein concentration. Running the BSA standard (reagents:A2) in other wells would be needed for that."}
